-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for H4Classes, H4Diagonal,
-- H4Bilinear, H4Proof (doc/h4.pdf): one entry per declaration.  Generated
-- from --opened after the locking of e_m and K(h, m) (28 Oct 2026,
-- handoff-5 §3a) and reviewed by kind (the union of all opened names).
-- Status: interface refactoring complete; the textual audit (rule 6: each
-- entry checked against its step in doc/h4.tex) is NOT yet done, so this
-- file records reproducible behaviour, not yet tightness.  Kinds as in truncation.opens and
-- cup.opens; in addition:
--   e_m and K(h, m) (EMMaps.KK.e, KMap.K / Kmap / cellS / conj) are opened only
--     in their "by definition" lemmas, H4Bilinear.Lev: conj-def (KMap.conj is
--     e_A ; F ; e_B^-1), conj-zero (e_0 is the band: KK.e -> EMSpace.loop0 ->
--     band-equiv, unband), K-zero (K(h,0) = map0), K-def, jA-def
--     (CupSquare.iota-eq is j_Z).  Lev locks eA, eB, K after loopK, so no
--     other entry opens them, nor cor11 / lemma9 / eqind / Deloop.Torsors.theorem2;
--   KMap.c0 = unband o g o band (H2.loop1, k1-inj), named in the text;
--   K(Z,2) as a type: KZ2 -> KK.K two -> EMSpace.K -> EMn.Kstage -> stage2 ->
--     EM2.K2 -> Deloop.Torsors.Tor, once each in 12 entries (DiagAt.Lift.contr,
--     back-lifts, sc, kf-comp, ENat.gs-x, nat-pt, hh, E-loop, E'-loop, e-nat,
--     BilAt.iota-back, key-pt).  Not a step of the text: the etaV defect of
--     doc/etav-lock-diagnostic.txt (addendum), the type of a bound variable
--     x : KZ2 put in whnf when x is forced.  Shown on an isolated case (an
--     identity step over x : KZ2 opens the whole chain; the same step for an
--     abstract pointed type opens nothing); for the 12 entries it is inferred
--     from the pattern (each binds a variable over KZ2), not shown one by one;
--   K(Z,1) (EM1.K1 -> TrivG.K -> img), the numerals and KZ2, KZ4, kz2, kz4, Zab
--     (library aliases), as in cup.opens;
-- Check: segd All.seg --opens h4.opens ; every line "nothing else opened".
